Question 23

What is one example of a disk scheduling technique?
SCAN
Sequential access
Relative path
Absolute path

Answer

That’s right! There are three main disk scheduling techniques. The first-come, first-served technique processes disk requests in the order they arrive, without considering the heads' current positions. The shortest-seek-time-first technique moves the heads by the smallest necessary amount in order to access the data. In the third type, SCAN disk scheduling, the read/write heads move in toward the spindle, then out toward the platter edge, then back toward the spindle, etc.



